WEBVTT

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.000
Tell an agent to fix the auth

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:06.460
bug,

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:07.940
and it won't ask which one.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:08.880
It will guess,

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:09.730
confidently,

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.380
and hand you a fix for something

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.680
you never asked about.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.210
There's no secret syntax that prevents this.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.930
Prompting is communication.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.440
If you can write a good bug

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.000
report,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.290
you already know how.

00:00:20.981 --> 00:00:22.721
A good task prompt says what you

00:00:22.721 --> 00:00:23.221
want,

00:00:23.221 --> 00:00:24.201
why it matters,

00:00:24.201 --> 00:00:25.831
and how success looks.

00:00:25.881 --> 00:00:28.881
The login endpoint rejects valid tokens when

00:00:28.881 --> 00:00:30.391
the session cache is cold.

00:00:30.441 --> 00:00:32.361
This test reproduces it.

00:00:32.361 --> 00:00:32.821
Fix it,

00:00:32.821 --> 00:00:35.011
and keep every auth test passing.

00:00:35.021 --> 00:00:36.501
Leave out the file path;

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.351
the agent can find that itself.

00:00:38.541 --> 00:00:40.161
Give it what tools can't:

00:00:40.161 --> 00:00:41.121
the symptom,

00:00:41.121 --> 00:00:41.971
the domain,

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:42.891
the intent.

00:00:43.685 --> 00:00:44.965
Then say what not to do.

00:00:44.965 --> 00:00:46.845
Agents are eager optimisers.

00:00:46.845 --> 00:00:47.965
Ask for a fix,

00:00:47.965 --> 00:00:49.895
and you might get a rewritten module,

00:00:49.945 --> 00:00:52.025
three new dependencies and a changed public

00:00:52.025 --> 00:00:52.875
interface.

00:00:53.045 --> 00:00:55.025
Constraints are the guardrails on the bridge.

00:00:55.025 --> 00:00:56.275
No new dependencies.

00:00:56.685 --> 00:00:58.455
Don't touch the public interface.

00:00:58.505 --> 00:01:00.075
Stay inside this folder.

00:01:00.866 --> 00:01:02.966
Build a dashboard with live metrics,

00:01:02.966 --> 00:01:03.606
roles,

00:01:03.606 --> 00:01:05.286
and exports isn't a prompt,

00:01:05.286 --> 00:01:06.356
it's a project.

00:01:06.386 --> 00:01:07.806
Split it into small,

00:01:07.806 --> 00:01:08.986
verifiable steps,

00:01:08.986 --> 00:01:10.186
the data model,

00:01:10.186 --> 00:01:11.236
then the endpoint,

00:01:11.306 --> 00:01:12.336
then the filtering,

00:01:12.466 --> 00:01:13.356
then the view.

00:01:13.386 --> 00:01:15.976
Each one checked before the next begins.

00:01:16.066 --> 00:01:17.916
And when tasks are independent,

00:01:17.966 --> 00:01:20.086
say so and let sub -agents run

00:01:20.086 --> 00:01:20.976
them in parallel.

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:23.800
For anything bigger than a small fix,

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:25.310
ask for a plan first.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:27.100
Don't change any code yet.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:28.210
Read the files,

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:29.910
and tell me what you'll touch and

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.030
how you'll verify it.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.730
A wrong assumption caught in a short

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.630
plan costs one sentence.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:36.150
Caught in a giant diff,

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.700
it costs the whole diff.

00:01:38.478 --> 00:01:40.358
Your first prompt won't be perfect.

00:01:40.358 --> 00:01:41.718
When the output is wrong,

00:01:41.718 --> 00:01:43.268
ask what you failed to say.

00:01:43.318 --> 00:01:45.888
The agent's output is the error message.

00:01:45.898 --> 00:01:47.828
Your prompt is the stack trace.

00:01:47.838 --> 00:01:50.068
You're debugging your own communication.

00:01:51.065 --> 00:01:52.445
Try speaking your prompts.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.755
Typing is tiring,

00:01:54.005 --> 00:01:56.635
so typed prompts shrink and lose context.

00:01:56.905 --> 00:01:58.825
Speaking costs almost nothing,

00:01:58.825 --> 00:02:00.425
so you tell the whole story of

00:02:00.425 --> 00:02:01.105
the bug.

00:02:01.105 --> 00:02:02.745
And when words fail,

00:02:02.745 --> 00:02:03.505
show it.

00:02:03.505 --> 00:02:05.525
A screenshot of a broken layout says

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.575
more than three paragraphs about padding.

00:02:08.373 --> 00:02:08.973
Finally,

00:02:08.973 --> 00:02:10.273
treat prompts as code.

00:02:10.273 --> 00:02:12.173
Save the ones that work as skills

00:02:12.173 --> 00:02:13.703
and slash commands,

00:02:13.813 --> 00:02:15.833
versioned in git and reviewed like anything

00:02:15.833 --> 00:02:16.683
else.

00:02:16.733 --> 00:02:18.593
Prompting isn't a parlour trick.

00:02:18.593 --> 00:02:19.663
It's engineering.

00:02:19.753 --> 00:02:20.713
Next up:

00:02:20.713 --> 00:02:21.293
local,

00:02:21.293 --> 00:02:22.943
commercial and hybrid models.
